<article class="env-proposition" id="DD1683">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/DD1683">Proposition <span data-tag="DD1683">4.3.2.15</span>.</a> Suppose given a diagram of $\infty $-categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \calC \rightarrow \calD ' \stackrel{p}{\leftarrow } \calD , \]
</div>
  <p> where $p$ is an inner fibration. Let $\calC ^{0}$ be a full subcategory of $\calC $. Let $\calK \subseteq \bHom _{\calD '}(\calC , \calD )$ be the full subcategory spanned by those functors $F: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ which are $p$-left Kan extensions of $F | \calC ^{0}$. Let $\calK ' \subseteq \bHom _{\calD '}(\calC ^{0}, \calD )$ be the full subcategory spanned by those functors $F_0: \calC ^{0} \rightarrow \calD $ with the property that, for each object $C \in \calC $, the induced diagram $ \calC ^{0}_{/C} \rightarrow \calD $ has a $p$-colimit. Then the restriction functor $\calK \rightarrow \calK '$ is a trivial fibration of simplicial sets. </p>
</article>